Name:
Nicholas Wachter

Data Description:
This data set is a grocery data set. Each entry is a customer ID, the date, and a single item. For the purposes of this
assignment I combined all of the items for a given customer ID and put that on one line so that each line is a list of
items that one customer bought.

Link:
https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/heeraldedhia/groceries-dataset

Data Interpretation:
From this data set I learned that people buy a lot of whole milk. Whole milk was highly correlated with several other
items in the dataset. The second most highly correlated item was was 'other vegetables'. I also found it interesting
that many times where A was likely to occur when B was there that the reverse was also true, B was likely to occur when
A was there.

Instructions:
Run in terminal with 'python3 apriori.py <csv file> <minsup> <minconf>'

No known problems.
